## Implementation Hygiene

- keep files focused and split them when they become hard to scan
- review changed file sizes before commit and record the split/keep decision
  when a file becomes mechanically large
- search for duplicate request builders, query builders, prompt rendering,
  signer/nonce handling, validation rules, and result formatting before commit
- respect local package boundaries and DDD rules; provider, database,
  transport, AI, and runtime DTOs must not leak across forbidden boundaries
- keep entrypoints boring: wiring belongs there, business rules do not
- avoid vague `helpers`, `utils`, `common`, `shared`, or `base` buckets unless
  the repo deliberately owns that convention and review accepts it

